ahhh the tyro meets Mac the Knife ... just kidding. the following was
going to get a spoiler alert but i've reconsidered since i think it
is necessary information needed to get beyond the early levels:
Elbereth is the name of the fairest of elves. this is appreciated by
merry middle-earthers who know that the mention of her name will turn
evil for a spell. in the dungeon, engraving Elbereth (with a steady
hand, check your writing habits!) will turn monsters (all non-@'s with
the exception of worms since they are beneath it, i think). stand on the
word giving the monster a chance to see it and it will turn (while the
word is intact). while "turned" the monsters will flee from you and you
may strike them at will. eventually (sometimes too soon!) they will turn
back. pets are exempt from the word also, i think.

you can engrave with your fingers, thus writing in the dust. this is
effective but prone to smudging. you may engrave with weapons at the
cost of dulling the engraving weapon and usually, unless the weapon is
specially enchanted, you will not complete the spelling of Elbereth.
the weapon has been wasted (that's good, right?) but the word isn't
effective unless its spelled correctly in its entirety. orcs throw
black knives although you may not see the orc. if you leave the weapon
behind the orc will simply pick it up again and re-use it, therefore you
should dispose of the weapon. wasn't it nice that the orc gave it to
you instead of using it on you in hand-to-hand combat? if you happen to
collect a set of these weapons you may consider finishing your
unfinished business! when Elbereth is carved into the rock it is
significantly more enduring ...
other items may be used to engrave the written word with various
effects. engraving does not run the risk of sticky-cursing unless you
wield the engraving tool. Elbereth does not prevent missile attacks or
exempt you from stupid mistakes but it may prolong your game and ease
the frustration. my guess is that even the best players who seemingly
walz thru the dungeon use this strategy on occasion.

